Allure Hair Studio Promotional Booklet Design

What we need

A promotional booklet that showcases the salon's services, team, and overall vibe. This should work for handing out in the Cherry Creek area and for sharing digitally. The main thing is making it feel welcoming and professional at the same time, something that reflects their 28 years in business without looking dated.

Who we're targeting

People in Denver looking for quality hair care. Most clients are professionals who care about their appearance and are willing to pay for good service. They're into premium products like Redken and appreciate when stylists actually know what they're doing. The tone should be warm but not cheesy.

Design direction

Stick with what they already have - soft blush pink as the main color, warm neutrals, and clean typography. Nothing too flashy. Modern but timeless. White space is important, don't crowd the pages.

Typography

Headers need to feel elegant but readable. A slight serif works well for that premium touch. Body text should be clean and easy to scan. Make sure different text levels are clearly distinguished so the layout doesn't feel messy.

Content sections we need

Cover page with salon branding, about section with the history and values, services overview with starting prices, team profiles with photos, product highlights, and contact info. Keep each section consistent with margins and spacing.

Images

Only use real photos from the salon. No stock images for main visuals. All images should be high-res and match the overall color treatment. Standardize aspect ratios so nothing gets awkwardly cropped.

Services to include

Hair extensions (hand-tied method), cuts and styling for all hair types, color services (full color, gloss, balayage, highlights), Brazilian Blowout treatment. Each service needs a short description and where applicable, starting price range. Keep technical terms simple.

Team profiles

Nicole Blackburn (owner, 28 years experience), Rebekah O'Neill (stylist and color specialist), and Samuel Jordan (barber at neighboring suite). Each needs a headshot and a 2-3 sentence bio that sounds human, not corporate.

Brand assets

Make sure to use the salon logo, brand colors with hex codes, and general messaging guidelines. All assets should be provided in editable formats so they can be updated later.

File formats

PDF for printing, editable source files, PNG for digital use, and JPEG for email. Label everything clearly with version numbers.

Quality check

Proofread everything before sending. Images should be clean without compression artifacts. Run through the final layout on different devices to make sure it looks good everywhere.
